message: "If you use this study, its code or its data, please cite it as below."
title: "Who gains most from AI? Logical reasoning as an amplifier of LLM-assisted performance (Logic x AI)"
type: software
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-11-05"
license: MIT
authors:
  - given-names: "KEYUR SHAILESHKUMAR"
    family-names: "PATEL"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-5261-043X"
    affiliation: "MSc Artificial Intelligence student, Department of Computer Science, Brunel University London, UK; Independent researcher"
abstract: >-
  A preregistered computational study testing whether logical reasoning
  predicts who gains most from an AI assistant. 28 open-weight language
  models in 3 reasoning modes act as solvers; an assistant AI helps them,
  with planted errors on half of the hard items. Conducted independently;
  not an official Brunel University London project.
keywords:
  - human-AI collaboration
  - logical reasoning
  - large language models
  - preregistration
  - open science
